# Software-project request phrase vocabulary (issues #1138, #1175).
#
# The object-phrase discipline of rust/src/solver_handlers/
# software_project_phrases.rs reads every surface from this file — the words
# that close an authoring verb's object noun phrase (so the artifact kind is
# the head the verb governs, never an incidental modifier), the determiners
# and benefactives that may lead the phrase without belonging to it, and the
# punctuation that ends a phrase or a sentence. The recognition algorithm is
# compiled; the vocabulary is data, one meaning per table, so extending the
# languages covered needs no Rust change. Every record is defined by the
# statement function-word genus — these surfaces carry grammatical structure,
# not lexical content.
#
# The word-internal character table declares `lexeme en`, `lexeme ru` and
# `lexeme es` with no surfaces on purpose — spaced scripts have no character
# that cuts a token at any position. ASCII punctuation inside a token is part
# of a name ("a Node.js service"), so listing it there would split names.

meanings
  software_object_boundary_word
    defined-by statement_function_word
    role software_object_boundary_word
    lexeme en
      words about and but by for from i in into it of or please so that they to using via we when where which who with
      words without
    lexeme zh 从 但 关于 和 或 那 请 所以 使用 谁 他们 它 到 的 为 通过 我们 无论 哪个 哪里 什么时候 与 经由 在
    lexeme es
      words a asi con cual cuando de desde dentro donde ello ellos en nosotros o para "por favor" que quien sobre sin
      words usando via y yo
    lexeme ru в для и из или которая которое который которые когда на от с чтобы
    lexeme hi और जो के को से में या
  software_object_lead_word
    defined-by statement_function_word
    role software_object_lead_word
    lexeme en a an the this that these those my your our me us please
    lexeme ru эта эти те мой твой наш мне нам пожалуйста
    lexeme hi एक यह वह ये वे मेरा तुम्हारा हमारा मुझे हमें कृपया
    lexeme zh 一个 这 那 这些 那些 我的 你的 我们的 我 我们 请
    lexeme es "por favor" el esos este estos la mi nos nuestro tu un una
  software_object_lead_bigram
    defined-by statement_function_word
    role software_object_lead_bigram
    lexeme en "for me" "for us" "to me" "to us"
    lexeme ru "для меня" "для нас"
    lexeme hi "मेरे लिए" "हमारे लिए"
    lexeme zh 给我 给我们 对我 对我们
    lexeme es "para mí" "para nosotros" "a mí" "a nosotros"
  software_object_boundary_character
    defined-by statement_function_word
    role software_object_boundary_character
    lexeme en "," ";" "." "?" "!" ":" "(" ")" "[" "]"
    lexeme zh "，" "。" "？" "！" "；" "：" "、"
    lexeme hi "।"
    
    lexeme ru "," ";" "." "?" "!" ":" "(" ")" "[" "]"
    lexeme es "," ";" "." "?" "!" ":" "(" ")" "[" "]"
  software_object_word_internal_character
    defined-by statement_function_word
    role software_object_word_internal_character
    lexeme zh "，" "。" "？" "！" "；" "：" "、"
    lexeme hi "।"
    lexeme en
    lexeme ru
    lexeme es
  software_sentence_end_character
    defined-by statement_function_word
    role software_sentence_end_character
    lexeme en "." "?" "!" ";" ":"
    lexeme zh "。" "？" "！" "；"
    lexeme hi "।"
    
    lexeme ru "." "?" "!" ";" ":"
    lexeme es "." "?" "!" ";" ":"
